WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.180
Last time we talked,

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.770
you were very candid about Twitter.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.603
And how --

00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:06.436
Yeah.

00:00:06.436 --> 00:00:07.470
You've been having some
issues with your Twitter

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.330
account because

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.680
like some of us

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.160
you like to have a drink or two

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.760
and then get on Twitter.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.593
And that can --

00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:15.495
Yeah.

00:00:15.495 --> 00:00:16.328
Lead to issues.

00:00:16.328 --> 00:00:17.419
I've deleted my Twitter account.

00:00:17.419 --> 00:00:18.252
(laughter)

00:00:18.252 --> 00:00:19.085
You deleted it?

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:19.918
Yeah.

00:00:19.918 --> 00:00:20.751
On my own merit,

00:00:20.751 --> 00:00:21.584
like, no one told me,

00:00:21.584 --> 00:00:22.417
"Kiersey, you should get off Twitter."

00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:23.600
I just deleted it.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.520
I just -- it's so

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.830
much going on.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.939
And it's toxic or something.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:29.772
[Conan] Yes.

00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:30.700
It's like high school, yeah.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.160
I can't.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.020
I can't do it.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:33.853
Yeah.

00:00:33.853 --> 00:00:34.686
I think, I think you're --

00:00:34.686 --> 00:00:36.810
I think you have the right approach.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.419
You described Twitter

00:00:38.419 --> 00:00:42.187
recently as being stuck at a bad party.

00:00:42.187 --> 00:00:43.020
Mhm.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:43.949
Is that how it feels to you?

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:45.230
One hundred percent.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:46.990
I realized when I was saying it, too,

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.790
that now you don't get stuck at parties

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.657
because we have, like,
chauffeurs on our phones --

00:00:53.657 --> 00:00:54.490
[Conan] Uh-huh, right.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.360
But when I was in high school,

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.010
I would always --

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.240
my friends were so bad.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.580
I was the good kid,

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.620
I just wanna be clear,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.610
and we would --

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.000
they'd be like, "It's fine, girl.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.450
Like, he's gonna drive us to the party.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.670
He doesn't drink.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.840
It's gonna be all good."

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.690
And then we get there and we're stuck.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.650
He's doing drugs.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.320
Not drinking but he might as well be.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.153
Right.

00:01:13.153 --> 00:01:14.150
And then you're stuck at the party

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:15.190
and you're like, "I don't wanna be here.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:16.590
I hate everybody here.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.600
And I keep coming back every weekend."

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.149
And that's what Twitter feels like to me.

00:01:20.149 --> 00:01:20.982
(laughter)

00:01:20.982 --> 00:01:22.117
Every time I'm there, I'm like,

00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:23.110
"Why did I come back?"

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:23.943
And I'm stuck.

00:01:23.943 --> 00:01:24.783
Right.

00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:25.616
You know.

00:01:25.616 --> 00:01:26.449
That sounds rough, Kiersey.

00:01:26.449 --> 00:01:28.670
Let me tell you what my experience was.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:30.869
Nobody invited me to a party!

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:32.640
(laughter)

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.780
Nobody!

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.640
No! That's the thing.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.010
Nobody was ever invited to the party.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:37.843
It's not --

00:01:37.843 --> 00:01:39.660
It's not a party anyone's invited to.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.976
It's like a party that ends
because you hear gunshots.

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:43.240
Yeah. Oh, well --

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.073
Those are the parties I was at.

00:01:44.073 --> 00:01:44.906
That's --

00:01:44.906 --> 00:01:45.739
that's different.

00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:46.572
Okay, yeah.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:47.405
Yeah.

00:01:47.405 --> 00:01:48.238
No, no, I didn't --

00:01:48.238 --> 00:01:49.071
Different high school we
went to, it sounds like.

00:01:49.071 --> 00:01:49.904
It sounds --

00:01:49.904 --> 00:01:50.737
well, first of all,

00:01:50.737 --> 00:01:51.630
we went to different high schools,

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.790
but I think, and I will
be honest with you,

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.440
there were no gunshots going off in

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.590
Brookline, Massachusetts, let me say that.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.812
But --

00:02:00.812 --> 00:02:01.845
Well, those are the best parties.

00:02:01.845 --> 00:02:03.460
At the same time,

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.810
if I had gone to your high school,

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:05.850
guess what?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.524
No one would have invited me to a party!

00:02:07.524 --> 00:02:08.440
(laughter)

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.273
That's --

00:02:09.273 --> 00:02:10.635
I would have.

00:02:10.635 --> 00:02:11.547
I would have invited you.

00:02:11.547 --> 00:02:12.943
You would have invited me to a party?

00:02:12.943 --> 00:02:13.776
And maybe you could have
been the designated driver

00:02:13.776 --> 00:02:15.644
and I wouldn't feel the way that I feel.

00:02:15.644 --> 00:02:17.270
If you would have invited me to the party,

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.103
people would have said,

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:19.931
"Why'd you bring that
weird white lady with you?"

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:22.640
(laughter)

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.757
White mom at the party.

00:02:23.757 --> 00:02:25.457
(laughter)

00:02:25.457 --> 00:02:27.309
"What's with the weird old white lady?

00:02:27.309 --> 00:02:28.560
What is she doing here?"

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.977
(laughter)

